{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"toolshed_web_search","tool":"call_web_search","arguments":{"fast_mode":false,"web_search_instructions":"Find the current Scalable Press API documentation relevant to creating designs, quotes/orders, test/sandbox behavior, and authentication. Focus on exact API endpoints and request/response payloads for DTG apparel as of 2026, including whether test API keys or test mode prevent real fulfillment. Return source URLs and concise implementation details."},"result":null,"error":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"toolshed_web_search","tool":"call_web_search","arguments":{"fast_mode":false,"web_search_instructions":"Find the current Scalable Press API documentation relevant to creating designs, quotes/orders, test/sandbox behavior, and authentication. Focus on exact API endpoints and request/response payloads for DTG apparel as of 2026, including whether test API keys or test mode prevent real fulfillment. Return source URLs and concise implementation details."},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Research Report: Scalable Press API Documentation for DTG Apparel\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nScalable Press offers a comprehensive API suite for direct-to-garment (DTG) apparel, encompassing design creation, quoting, ordering, and authentication. The API supports test modes to prevent real fulfillment during development, ensuring a seamless integration process.\n\n## Key Findings\n\n- **Finding 1:** The Design API allows for the creation of design objects by uploading artwork files with specified dimensions and placements, which can be used for quotes, mockups, and orders. ([scalablepress.com](https://scalablepress.com/api?utm_source=openai))\n\n- **Finding 2:** The Quote API provides exact pricing for orders, distinguishing between order-ready and quote-only scenarios based on the completeness of the provided information. ([scalablepress.com](https://scalablepress.com/docs/?utm_source=openai))\n\n- **Finding 3:** The Order API enables the placement and management of print-and-ship orders, including functionalities for retrieving, canceling, and reprinting orders. ([apis.apievangelist.com](https://apis.apievangelist.com/store/scalablepress-order-api/?utm_source=openai))\n\n- **Finding 4:** Authentication is handled via HTTP Basic authentication, requiring the API key as the password, and the API supports test modes to prevent real fulfillment during development. ([scalablepress.com](https://scalablepress.com/docs/?utm_source=openai))\n\n---\n\n## Detailed Source Analysis\n\n### Source 1: API Documentation\n\n- **URL:** ([scalablepress.com](https://scalablepress.com/docs/?utm_source=openai))\n\n- **Domain:** scalablepress.com\n\n- **Publication Date:** Date not specified\n\n- **Source Type:** Commercial\n\n- **Credibility:** High (Official documentation from Scalable Press)\n\n**Summary:**\n\nThe API Documentation provides detailed information on the Quote API, which allows users to obtain exact quotes before placing orders. It outlines three possible outcomes: order-ready, quote-only, and error, depending on the completeness and validity of the provided information. The documentation also describes the process for generating bulk quotes, which offer flexibility for multiple printing orders and split shipping. Additionally, it covers custom order features such as selecting shipping options, providing custom packing slips, and custom white labeling. Authentication headers are required for API access.\n\n**Key Data Points:**\n\n- Three possible quote outcomes: order-ready, quote-only, and error.\n\n- Bulk quotes support multiple printing orders and split shipping.\n\n- Custom order features include shipping options, packing slips, and white labeling.\n\n**Notable Quotes:**\n\n> \"The Quote API lets you get an exact quote before placing an order.\"\n\n> \"Authentication headers are required.\"\n\n---\n\n### Source 2: Developer API | Print & Ship Products with Simple API Calls\n\n- **URL:** ([scalablepress.com](https://scalablepress.com/api?utm_source=openai))\n\n- **Domain:** scalablepress.com\n\n- **Publication Date:** Date not specified\n\n- **Source Type:** Commercial\n\n- **Credibility:** High (Official developer API page from Scalable Press)\n\n**Summary:**\n\nThis source introduces the Scalable Press API, emphasizing its capability to programmatically send customized products such as t-shirts, mugs, phone cases, and posters. It highlights features like no minimum order quantities, fast turnaround times, multiple production centers, and quality processes. The API allows for the creation of design objects by uploading artwork files with specified dimensions and placements, which can be used to get quotes, create mockups, and place orders. An example request for creating a design object is provided, demonstrating the API's functionality.\n\n**Key Data Points:**\n\n- No minimum order quantities.\n\n- Orders typically ship within 1-3 business days.\n\n- Multiple production centers in CA, IN, and PA.\n\n**Notable Quotes:**\n\n> \"We believe ordering customized products should be as simple and inexpensive as ordering normal products. This starts with our API.\"\n\n> \"Create a design object. Upload an artwork file, along with dimensions and placement specifications, to create a design object.\"\n\n---\n\n### Source 3: Scalable Press Order API\n\n- **URL:** ([apis.apievangelist.com](https://apis.apievangelist.com/store/scalablepress-order-api/?utm_source=openai))\n\n- **Domain:** apis.apievangelist.com\n\n- **Publication Date:** Date not specified\n\n- **Source Type:** Other\n\n- **Credibility:** Medium (Third-party API documentation)\n\n**Summary:**\n\nThe Scalable Press Order API allows users to place and manage print-and-ship orders. It exposes six operations across four paths, including retrieving all orders, placing an order, retrieving a single order, canceling an order, reprinting an order, and changing an order address. The API uses HTTP Basic authentication, requiring the private API key as the password. The base URL for the API is `https://api.scalablepress.com/v2`.\n\n**Key Data Points:**\n\n- Six operations: listOrders, createOrder, getOrder, cancelOrder, reprintOrder, changeOrderAddress.\n\n- Base URL: `https://api.scalablepress.com/v2`.\n\n- Authentication: HTTP Basic with API key as password.\n\n**Notable Quotes:**\n\n> \"Scalable Press Order API is one of 8 APIs that Scalable Press publishes on the APIs.io network.\"\n\n> \"Requests are made against a single base URL, `https://api.scalablepress.com`.\"\n\n---\n\n## Cross-Reference Analysis\n\n**Consensus Across Sources:**\n\n- All sources confirm that Scalable Press provides a comprehensive API suite for DTG apparel, including design creation, quoting, and ordering functionalities. ([scalablepress.com](https://scalablepress.com/docs/?utm_source=openai))\n\n- Authentication is consistently handled via HTTP Basic authentication, requiring the API key as the password. ([scalablepress.com](https://scalablepress.com/docs/?utm_source=openai))\n\n**Conflicting Information:**\n\n- No significant conflicting information was identified across the sources.\n\n**Information Gaps:**\n\n- Specific details regarding the test mode's behavior in preventing real fulfillment during development are not explicitly detailed in the provided sources.� "}],"_meta":{"openai/widgetSessionId":"7b58b007-c8c1-4a3a-a98d-59478454f07f"},"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
